<title>POLAND: Gdansk Institute Polish macroeconomic forecast.</title>
<headline>Gdansk Institute Polish macroeconomic forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest macroeconomic forecast for Poland from the independent Gdansk Market Economy Institute (IBnGR), based on data from the first quarter of 1997 and released on April 24.</p>
<p>Tel -- +48 58 41-3977, 41-1535, Fax -- +48 58 41-0620</p>
<p>POLISH INDICATORS - PCT CHANGE VS PREVIOUS PERIOD</p>
<p>				 *  RESULT	    FORECAST</p>
<p>				 *  1996	 1997	     1998</p>
<p> GDP TOTAL		   *   6.0	5.7 (5.4)     4.9 (4.8)</p>
<p>  FARMING OUTPUT	   *  -3.2	2.4 (4.5)    -2.4(-5.5)</p>
<p>  NON-FARMING OUTPUT     *   5.8	5.3 (5.7)     4.9 (5.3)</p>
<p>   INDUSTRIAL		*   7.7	6.3 (7.6)     6.3 (7.7)</p>
<p>   CONSTRUCTION	    *   3.9	7.7 (6.3)     6.1 (4.8)</p>
<p> DOMESTIC DEMAND	   *   9.7	8.7 (7.8)     6.8 (5.9)</p>
<p>  PRIVATE CONSUMPTION    *   8.1	6.7 (6.2)     5.3 (4.6)</p>
<p>  PUBLIC CONSUMPTION     *   3.4	4.0 (3.9)     2.0 (2.0)</p>
<p> EXPORTS (PCT GROWTH)    *   7.4     10.1 (7.9)     9.5(10.7)</p>
<p> IMPORTS (PCT GROWTH)    *  24.2     17.9(14.1)    13.1(10.3)</p>
<p> TRADE GAP (PCT GDP)     *  -3.5     -5.9 (N/A)    -7.5 (N/A)</p>
<p> INVESTMENT (PCT OF GDP) *  19.0     21.0(19.7)    22.7(21.2)</p>
<p> HOUSEHOLD SAVINGS	 *   9.5	8.5 (8.4)     7.9(10.5)</p>
<p> BUDGET DEFICIT (PCT GDP)*  -2.5     -2.6(-2.5)    -2.4(-2.4)</p>
<p> REAL WAGE GROWTH	  *   6.1	5.3 (4.6)     4.0 (4.0)</p>
<p> BROAD MONEY (PLN BLN)   * 135.9	164 (165)     193 (198)</p>
<p> GDP DEFLATOR		*  19.2     14.2(15.5)    14.0(13.0)</p>
<p> CPI (AVERAGE YEARLY)    *  19.9     15.4(16.3)    14.5(14.5)</p>
<p> PPI (AVERAGE YEARLY)    *  12.1     10.8 (N/A)    11.5 (N/A)</p>
<p> USD/PLN		     *   2.70     3.19(3.12)    3.63(3.56)</p>
<p> DEM/PLN		     *   1.79     1.85(N/A)     2.13(N/A)</p>
<p> STATE RESERVES(USD BLN) *  18.0     16.5(16.5)    16.0(16.0)</p>
<p> NET RESERVES (USD BLN)  *  21.8     19.8 (N/A)    22.8 (N/A)</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in brackets are previous forecasts done at the end of 1996. Household savings given as pct of income.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
